\name{cellucid_view_picture}
\alias{cellucid_view_picture}
\title{Take a picture of a view}
\usage{
cellucid_view_picture(
  viewer,
  height = 480,
  legend = TRUE,
  source = "figure",
  view,
  width = 640
)
}
\arguments{
\item{viewer}{A viewer \code{\link{cellucid_view}()} or \code{\link{cellucid_serve}()} returned.}
\item{height}{The height of the box the plot fits in, in pixels (source "export": of the box the figure is scaled into). A whole number (at least 100, at most 20000). Default \code{480}, the viewer's own.}
\item{legend}{Draw the color legend beside the plot (a figure picture; the screen has none). \code{TRUE} or \code{FALSE}. Default \code{TRUE}, the viewer's own.}
\item{source}{figure: one view drawn as the figure export draws it (points, legend; no overlay), with plain settings (no title, 12 px text, the screen's background). screen: the view's pane as the screen shows it now, overlays included (the moving flow caught at this instant), no legend; the view must be on screen. export: the figure Export would download now, with every Figure export setting (figure_export_set), scaled down into width \ifelse{latex}{<U+00D7>}{×} height (ask 1200 \ifelse{latex}{<U+00D7>}{×} 1200 or more to read a multi-panel figure's titles). One of \code{"figure"}, \code{"screen"}, \code{"export"}. Default \code{"figure"}, the viewer's own.}
\item{view}{The view: "View N" as the Compare views list numbers it; the selected view when left out. Not with source "export" (it draws what Export would). Text. Left out unless given (the viewer then chooses as its own control does).}
\item{width}{The width of the box the plot fits in, in pixels: the plot keeps the view's shape inside width \ifelse{latex}{<U+00D7>}{×} height, as the figure export frames it (the picture adds its margins and the legend). With source "export": the box the whole figure is scaled down into (never up). A whole number (at least 100, at most 20000). Default \code{640}, the viewer's own.}
}
\value{
A \code{cellucid_action_request}, at once and invisibly: the action is sent now, or when the viewer's channel opens.
\code{\link{cellucid_action_result}(request)} returns what it read: a list of \code{height} (The image's height in pixels), \code{label} (The name the view was given (view_rename), or null), \code{notes} (What the picture leaves out of what the view shows, or draws over it (a figure: an overlay it cannot draw; the screen: the legend; both: the highlighted cells drawn in the highlight's color over the coloring); for "export", first the figure's own size), \code{plot} (The plot's size in the image: the largest rectangle of the view's shape inside the width \ifelse{latex}{<U+00D7>}{×} height asked for; null for an "export" picture of every view), \code{png} (The image, base64-encoded PNG bytes (an agent receives it as an image)), \code{view} (The view drawn, by its name; null for an "export" picture of every view), \code{width} (The image's width in pixels). Cells in it are original positions (0-based rows of the dataset's obs).
}
\description{
A PNG of a view as the figure export draws it (points, legend), or as the screen shows it now (source "screen": the vector field overlay, the connectivity edges and a playing camera path's caption included, which a figure cannot draw), or the whole figure exactly as Export would download it now with the Figure export settings (source "export": size, frame, background, fonts, title, panel titles, legends, every view while Export all views is on: check a figure with it before the person downloads it); returned as base64; nothing is downloaded.
}
\details{
The viewer's action \code{view.picture} (Views). It reads, and changes nothing: it makes no step of the history.
}
\seealso{
\code{\link{cellucid_act}()} sends any action by its type, and \code{\link{cellucid_action_result}()}
collects its answer.
}
\examples{
if (interactive() && requireNamespace("SeuratObject", quietly = TRUE)) {
  data("pbmc_small", package = "SeuratObject")
  viewer <- cellucid_view(SeuratObject::UpdateSeuratObject(pbmc_small))
  request <- cellucid_view_picture(viewer)
  print(request)
  # cellucid_action_result(request) waits for what it read.
  cellucid_stop(viewer)
}
}
